# J7 — Findings triage & dismissal
# Walk findings, dismiss a false positive, suppress one, record a decision.
# Runs keylessly on demo findings. Judge: is dismissal/suppression state
# honest and durable — can the operator tell a SUPPRESSED finding from a
# GONE one?
name: Findings triage and dismissal
cwd: @TMP_TARGET
env-unset: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY OPENAI_API_KEY
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1
launch:
wait-for: 25 CHOOSE A TARGET
keys: d
wait-for: 90 run completed
keys: Escape
wait: 2
submit: findings
wait: 3
snap: findings-before
submit: open F-0001
wait: 3
snap: finding-open
ask: Finding detail — are dismiss / suppress / decision actions signposted from here, or does the operator have to guess verbs?
submit: decision false-positive not exploitable in this deployment
wait: 3
snap: decision-recorded
ask: Decision — was the human review decision recorded and acknowledged honestly (or was the verb syntax rejected with a helpful message)?
submit: suppress F-0002 --reason documentation-example --author operator --days 90
wait: 3
snap: suppress-attempt
ask: Suppress — did suppression require evidence/expiry as promised, and is the outcome stated plainly?
submit: findings
wait: 3
snap: findings-after
ask: After triage — can you tell the suppressed/dismissed finding from a GONE one in the list (distinct signifier, not silent disappearance)?
